          body: 'Sentence: “Driven by ambition, the young entrepreneur has worked tirelessly to build her startup.”\n\nStep 1, list every verb form: Driven, has worked, to build.\nStep 2, which is finite? “Has worked” shows tense (present perfect) and agrees with the singular subject “entrepreneur”. “Driven” is a past participle used as a modifier, and “to build” is an infinitive. Both are non-finite.\nStep 3, split “has worked”: “has” is the auxiliary, “worked” the lexical verb.\nStep 4, action or linking? “Worked” shows action. Transitive? Ask “worked what?” There is no object, so it is intransitive. (“To build” is transitive: it takes “her startup”.)\nResult: finite, intransitive “has worked”, with “to build her startup” explaining purpose.',
