            'Many adverbs end in -ly, but fast, hard, late and well do not, and “hardly” means barely, not hard.',
            'Frequency adverbs go before a main verb and after be; manner adverbs follow the verb or its object.',
            'Place focusing words like only and almost directly before the word they limit, because moving them changes the meaning.',
